# Samsara -- a Minecraft instance that happens to contain a project.
#
# WHY DENY-ALL-THEN-WHITELIST, rather than the usual list of exclusions:
# this repo's root is a live CurseForge *instance* directory, not a mod source
# tree. The game and the launcher continuously write files here that we do not
# own (saves, logs, caches, generated configs, downloaded jars), and new ones
# appear whenever a mod is added. A deny-list would silently start tracking
# whatever the next mod or launcher update drops in. Whitelisting means the
# repo contains the project and nothing else, by default.
#
# NOTE most published Minecraft .gitignore advice -- including KubeJS's own --
# targets MOD DEVELOPMENT (Gradle: build/, .gradle/, run/, Eclipse/IDEA files).
# None of that applies here: there is no build. The source IS the scripts and
# the datapack JSON, interpreted at runtime.

# 1. Ignore everything.
/*
/.*

# 2. Un-ignore the project.

# The repo's own metadata.
!/.gitignore
!/.gitattributes

# KubeJS: all of our actual source. Scripts (server/client/startup) plus the
# datapack JSON that defines the five custom realms -- dimension,
# dimension_type, worldgen/biome, worldgen/noise_settings.
!/kubejs/

# Project documentation and the agent brief. The project notes are the operational
# brief; the notes folder holds the design docs, the session handoff, and the offline
# test harness (test_routing.js), all of which are source.

# 3. Re-ignore things that live INSIDE the whitelisted trees.

# KubeJS writes its Mojang-mapping remapper cache and generated output here.
# Machine-specific, large, and regenerated on demand.
/kubejs/cache/
/kubejs/exported/

# Agent scratch state: per-session transcripts, local settings, tool caches.
# settings.local.json is explicitly the "not shared" settings file.

# OS metadata, anywhere in the tree.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately NOT tracked, and why. Each is already covered by the /* above;
# this is the reasoning, so nobody "helpfully" adds them later.
#
#   saves/                 71 MB of binary world data, and the biggest reason
#                          not to track it: the project notes' hard rule is that save
#                          files are never deleted or corrupted. Git operations
#                          (checkout, reset, stash) on a live world directory
#                          are exactly how that happens. Keep git away from it.
#   mods/                  Third-party jars. Versions are pinned in the project notes
#                          and reproducible from minecraftinstance.json; binary
#                          blobs in git are not how you distribute them. Also
#                          the project notes require asking before changing mods, and
#                          tracking them invites silent changes.
#   config/                Game-GENERATED per-mod tomls, rewritten on launch
#                          (it currently holds leftovers for Aether, Twilight
#                          Forest and Undergarden -- mods that are not even
#                          installed). Not source. If a config ever becomes
#                          load-bearing for the pack, it belongs in
#                          defaultconfigs/ and should be whitelisted then.
#   logs/, crash-reports/  Runtime output. Read constantly during testing --
#                          the project notes require checking logs/latest.log after
#                          every in-game test -- but never a source artifact.
#   local/                 KubeJS dev.properties: machine-local toggles.
#   rhino.local.properties Carries its own warning in the file: "please do not
#                          push this to version control".
#   minecraftinstance.json Launcher state: ~MBs of embedded Forge version JSON
#                          and per-file CDN URLs, rewritten by CurseForge.
#   .curseclient           Launcher instance UUID.
#   usercache.json         Contain a real player UUID and username. Not secret,
#   usernamecache.json     but personal data with no reason to be in history.
#   options.txt, imgui.ini Local client settings (keybinds, video, UI layout).
#   downloads/             Launcher download cache.
#   resourcepacks/         Empty, and client-side preference either way.
#   shaderpacks/
#   datapacks/             Empty: Samsara ships its datapack through
#                          kubejs/data/, which IS tracked.
#   defaultconfigs/        Empty today. Whitelist it if the pack ever ships
#                          default mod configs -- those WOULD be source.
